#!/bin/sh
# Redmi 8: the whole system is a disk image on the userdata partition, with
# its own partition table (p1 = /boot, p2 = /). Attach it as a loop device
# with partitions, so the root filesystem can be found by its UUID.
PREREQ=""
prereqs() { echo "$PREREQ"; }
case "$1" in prereqs) prereqs; exit 0 ;; esac
. /scripts/functions

part=/dev/disk/by-partlabel/userdata
i=0
while [ ! -e "$part" ] && [ $i -lt 60 ]; do sleep 0.5; i=$((i + 1)); done
[ -e "$part" ] || panic "OLIVE: no userdata partition"
losetup -j "$part" | grep -q . || losetup -P -f "$part"
udevadm settle 2>/dev/null || true
exit 0
